A number converter is a tool or program used to convert numbers from one form, system, or unit into another. It helps users easily change values without doing manual calculations. Number converters are commonly used in mathematics, computer programming, engineering, and daily activities.

Examples of number conversion include:

Decimal to Binary
Binary to Decimal
Decimal to Hexadecimal
Kilometers to Miles
Celsius to Fahrenheit
Currency conversion

A number converter usually includes:

An input field for entering the number
Options for selecting the conversion type
A convert button
A display area for showing the converted result

The main purpose of a number converter is to provide fast, accurate, and convenient conversions. It saves time and reduces errors when working with different number systems or measurement units.
